Subject: [PATCH] mfmediaengine: remove an unused topology-event variant cleanup

The topology-ready event handler declares a PROPVARIANT which is never
initialized or populated, then calls PropVariantClear on it. That function
reads the variant type and can release/free its payload. Clearing arbitrary
stack contents is not safe, even if the usual stack contents happen to be
VT_EMPTY or another harmless scalar type.

Remove the unused variable and cleanup, rather than initializing a value
which has no purpose. The event's topology status is obtained directly with
GetUINT32; no owned object or allocation is associated with this variable.
Notification ordering, locking, volume application and scrubbing are unchanged.

This is a pre-existing Wine defect also present in SE2-P1 and SE2-P3. It is
not an attribution of the Volare player stall to this code path. The extracted
topology-handler regression test diagnoses the old uninitialized read with
GCC's analyzer and verifies the fixed ready/not-ready notification behavior.
---
diff --git a/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c b/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c
--- a/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c
+++ b/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c
@@ -1120,7 +1120,6 @@
         case MESessionTopologyStatus:
         {
             UINT32 topo_status = 0;
-            PROPVARIANT value;
 
             IMFMediaEvent_GetUINT32(event, &MF_EVENT_TOPOLOGY_STATUS, &topo_status);
             if (topo_status != MF_TOPOSTATUS_READY)
@@ -1147,8 +1146,6 @@
 
             LeaveCriticalSection(&engine->cs);
 
-            PropVariantClear(&value);
-
             break;
         }
         case MESessionStarted:
